ork for the project's seafood safety and risk assessment objectives."}],B5=[{icon:Tc,title:"Marine Water Quality",desc:"Microbiological and water-quality assessment of coastal and nearshore waters using culture-based and MPN methods. Baseline data generated for the MSP and UrbanFisheries programmes supports detection of faecal indicator organisms across urbanization gradients. Ongoing interest in linking water-quality patterns to land-based inputs along the Kenyan coast."},{icon:xh,title:"Benthic Habitats",desc:"Support to benthic habitat mapping through laboratory analysis of sediment samples collected during the MSP Southeast Monsoon survey (12–18 August 2026). Sediment processing contributes to characterizing soft-bottom habitats across Kenya's north and south coast. This work forms part of the ecological dataset underpinning science-based marine spatial planning."},{icon:Sa,title:"Coastal Food Safety",desc:"Microbiological assessment of water and sediment in environments supporting small-scale coastal fisheries, contributing to UrbanFisheries seafood safety objectives. Interest in the occurrence and transfer of faecal indicator organisms and pathogens in nearshore production environments. Completed baselines now underpin the project's contaminant and risk assessment analyses."},{icon:wx,title:"Climate–Urbanization Impacts on Fisheries",desc:"Interest in how urban expansion and climate pressures reshape small-scale coastal fisheries livelihoods and seafood quality. Fieldwork spans rural-to-urban nearshore gradients sampled under the UrbanFisheries programme on both coasts. Focus on how laboratory baselines inform resilience assessments and management decisions."}],U5=[{label:"Completed",text:"Microbiological and water-quality baseline analysis for the MSP Southeast Monsoon survey (Aug 2026) — north & south coast stations."},{label:"Completed",text:"Water and sediment microbiological analysis for UrbanFisheries across north & south coast nearshore sites."},{label: