ratory analysis of water and sediment samples collected during the survey. The microbiological and water-quality baseline analysis has been completed, contributing to the project's broader oceanographic, biogeochemical, and plankton dataset.",tags:[{label:"Water Quality Sampling",done:!0},{label:"Sediment Analysis",done:!0},{label:"Microbiological Baseline Assessment",done:!0},{label:"Multidisciplinary Field Survey",done:!1},{label:"ISO/IEC 17025:2017 Lab Standards",done:!1}]},{icon:ba,title:"UrbanFisheries Project",subtitle:"3-year transdisciplinary project · East Africa coastal fisheries · Ongoing",image:Kv.water,alt:"Nearshore water sampling along an East African coastal gradient for the UrbanFisheries project",status:"Ongoing",body:["UrbanFisheries is an ongoing, 3-year transdisciplinary project examining the intersection of urbanization, climate change, and small-scale coastal fisheries (SSF) in East Africa — covering SSF livelihood resilience, effects of urban environments on seafood availability and quality, and challenges and opportunities for SSF under future climate and urban pressures. Fieldwork spans rural-to-urban nearshore gradients, with sampling of key fishery species for micronutrient, stable isotope, and contaminant analysis."],findings:["Completed water and sediment microbiological analysis across rural-to-urban nearshore gradients on both coasts.","Baselines now underpin the project's seafood-safety and risk-assessment objectives."],contribution:"I sampled and analyzed water and sediment samples from both north and south coast sites. This microbiological and water-quality work has been completed, forming part of the groundwork underpinning the project's ongoing seafood safety and risk assessment objectives.",tags:[{label:"Nearshore Ecological Sampling",done:!0},{label:"Water/Sediment Analysis",done:!0},{label:"Microbiological Assessment",done:!0},{label:"Coastal Food Security Research",done:!1}]}],W5=[{icon:Tc,title:"Marine Water Quality Monitori